TASK-181 / TASK-182 runtime harness: palette host completion and Backspace after
moving the caret off an inline completion, through the field editor's real
key bindings. Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task181-182-harness.patch
    xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    OUT="$PWD/.derived-logs/task182"; mkdir -p "$OUT"
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify182 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # wait for the "done" line in $OUT/verify.log (about 15 s), then kill that pid
    git apply -R docs/harness/task181-182-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

Seeds three sleeping www.youtube.com/watch?v=N tabs (listed, never loaded) and
a typed visit to yourstore.example, then sends keys to the field editor with
`firstResponder.keyDown(with:)`, so Cmd+Right goes through the key bindings.

    H1  Cmd+T, "you": field youtube.com with "tube.com" selected; rows: the
        site root, the verbatim row, Your Store, the three videos
    B1  Cmd+Right: caret at 11, nothing selected
    B2  Backspace: "youtube.co" (the old code reset the field to "you")
    U1  Cmd+T, "youtube.com/w": URL-level completion youtube.com/watch?v=1
    U2  Backspace with the completion selected: "youtube.com/w"
    L1-L3  same, then Left and Backspace: "youtube.com/atch?v=1"

Each step logs the field, its selection and the rows' label texts (hidden
labels included, so every row also lists "Switch to Tab"). The cacheDisplay
SHOT comes out blank for the glass palette; use screencapture for pixels.

